{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/jyx0ra1s","slide":4,"text":"5:00–5:45 · Experiment overview\nBoth cohorts use the Qwen 3.5 backbone, Reasoner/Engineer/Critic roles, Lean checking and lemma search, with every turn stored as JSON.\nEasy asks the team to solve one complete theorem directly: 100 runs across 10 tasks, with 56 independently verified final proofs.\nMedium introduces 4–6 connected subgoals and explicit return routes: 20 runs across two tasks, up to 200 agent steps, with no verified final proof.\nCaveat: difficulty and orchestration changed together, so this is not a controlled architecture comparison.\nSources: dataset/Lean/metadata.json; docs/lean_easy_failure_report/public/data/report_snapshot.json; data/experiments/qwen_medium_subgoals_v1/summary.json."}
