{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/i107q5of","slide":5,"text":"5:45–7:00 · Easy-run behaviors\nThe stored topology is overwhelmingly forward-only: 97/100 connected-linear traces and no Engineer→Reasoner or Critic→Engineer repair returns.\nThis does not mean no repair occurred. In 17/56 solved runs, the Engineer repaired its own candidate after a failed Lean check; earlier agents did not revise their work.\nRepeated search: deterministic post-hoc Reasoner-query similarity audit. Normalize NFKC/case/punctuation, split camelCase, map iff variants, then character-trigram Dice ≥0.80 against an earlier same-trial query; sustained means at least three recurrent follow-ups. Result: 12/100, 11 unsolved. This is not the CSV perseverated field.\nStatement drift: five Engineers changed the requested theorem; four became silent failures.\nApproval by trust: 30/59 accepted submissions had zero Critic check_lean calls.\nHand-audited trace: easy_fatem_115_t2 — changed target passes, requested target fails, Critic approves. Repeated-search example: easy_fatem_019_t5. Positive local-repair control: easy_fatem_012_t3.\nSources: docs/lean_easy_failure_report/public/data/report_snapshot.json; data/analysis/lean_easy_failure_patterns.csv; data/analysis/lean_easy_failure_reviews.jsonl; docs/lean_easy_failure_report/public/data/lean_easy_failure_traces.json; raw traces under data/batch."}
