{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/gnmp4jqx","slide":7,"text":"8:10–8:50 · Next experiments\nFirst, run matched comparisons: roles, models, tools, frameworks and parallel subagents on the same tasks and budgets.\nSecond, scale the evidence pipeline from deterministic JSON metrics to human audit, an optional advanced-model second opinion, and a cross-cohort dashboard.\nThird, transfer the trace schema to STARGAZER: 100 synthetic and 20 archival astrophysics systems with physical validation anchors.\nClose: these results identify workflow mechanisms. They do not yet establish that one architecture is superior.\nConcept source: internal concept note."}
